Return Codes
------------

  1. Say you have a command that fails rarely. In order to debug it you need to
     capture its output but it can be time consuming to get a failure run.
     Write a bash script that runs the following script until it fails and
     captures its standard output and error streams to files and prints
     everything at the end. Bonus points if you can also report how many runs
     it took for the script to fail.

          #!/usr/bin/env bash

          n=$(( RANDOM % 100 ))

          if [[ $n -eq 42 ]]; then
             echo "Something went wrong"
             >&2 echo "The error was using magic numbers"
             exit 1
          fi

          echo "Everything went according to plan"


