Profiling
=========

Even if your code functionally behaves as you would expect, that might not be
good enough if it takes all your CPU or memory in the process. Algorithms
classes often teach big _O_ notation but not how to find hot spots in your
programs. Since premature optimization is the root of all evil
(https://wiki.c2.com/?PrematureOptimization), you should learn about profilers
and monitoring tools. They will help you understand which parts of your program
are taking most of the time and/or resources so you can focus on optimizing
those parts.

