   • Git for Computer Scientists
     (https://eagain.net/articles/git-for-computer-scientists/) is a short
     explanation of Git's data model, with less pseudocode and more fancy
     diagrams than these lecture notes.
   • Git from the Bottom Up
     (https://jwiegley.github.io/git-from-the-bottom-up/) is a detailed
     explanation of Git's implementation details beyond just the data model,
     for the curious.
   • How to explain git in simple words
     (https://smusamashah.github.io/blog/2017/10/14/explain-git-in-simple-words)
   • Learn Git Branching (https://learngitbranching.js.org/) is a browser-based
     game that teaches you Git.


